WEBVTT

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.063
Vanish!

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.982
Vanish?

00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:51.361
I know the ball will bounce up.

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:54.989
But with all this dust,

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:57.200
I don't know where it'll come from!

00:02:00.036 --> 00:02:02.163
H-He dodged it!

00:02:03.707 --> 00:02:06.084
My eyes are getting used to it!

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:07.252
Don't get ahead of yourself!

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:09.671
This will finish it!

00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:10.588
Vanish!

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:15.218
I need to do something about this dust!

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.352
I see it!

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:28.106
Oh, no! It disappeared again!

00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:31.026
You're a moron.

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:37.699
N-No matter where the ball bounces...

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.952
Let me teach you my motto!

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.540
An eye for an eye!

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.460
Oh, I'm <i>so </i>scared!

00:03:09.064 --> 00:03:15.070
"The Night Before the Battle"

00:03:18.823 --> 00:03:20.742
They're late.

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:23.661
Why did you only let the losers go?

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:28.458
Calm down, Kirihara-<i>kun</i>.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.419
Throwing a fit won't do any good.

00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:37.425
Hey, looks like they're back.

00:03:48.395 --> 00:03:51.690
Only the middle schoolers came back.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.192
Looks like there were some upsets.

00:03:57.654 --> 00:03:59.572
Well, look at you guys.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.449
You've got more presence now.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:05.537
Those are some nice looks on their faces, huh?

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:09.541
The losers' revolution has begun.

00:04:13.837 --> 00:04:15.380
Good work, guys.

00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:18.425
Where's Kintaro?

00:04:18.425 --> 00:04:19.718
Right here!

00:04:24.347 --> 00:04:26.641
You okay now, buddy?

00:04:29.144 --> 00:04:30.395
Wait...

00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:32.814
You forgot this.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.275
Don't lose it, runt.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:37.652
Thanks!

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.796
That's...

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.799
The U-17 Japanese team representatives...

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.511
Numbers one through ten.

00:05:07.474 --> 00:05:11.061
--Hey, buddy! Are you okay?
--Fools are so quick to let go of their pride...

00:05:11.061 --> 00:05:12.645
Hey, Tokugawa.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.482
I hope you've improved a bit.

00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:23.490
Hey, buddy! Wake up!

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:27.911
What do you think you're doing?!

00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:30.455
Hey.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.001
Why don't you play us next?

00:05:36.544 --> 00:05:37.629
Oh?

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:45.470
Hold up!

00:05:46.888 --> 00:05:50.558
Teach us to play, too.

00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:55.855
This training camp's getting lively.

00:05:57.065 --> 00:05:58.274
Irie-<i>kun</i>.

00:05:59.109 --> 00:06:02.445
But he won't take it lying down.

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:06.408
Don't get too full of yourselves, brats.

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.002
You have one day.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:21.131
I'll state our terms.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:28.596
Create your own lineup including
the middle schoolers.

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:31.558
Any objections, you bungling coaches?

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:34.519
Not if they're all right with it.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.897
Good. Then it's decided.

00:06:38.732 --> 00:06:43.278
Tomorrow morning, we'll hold shuffle
matches for spots on the Japanese team!

00:06:44.154 --> 00:06:45.739
I'm fine with that,

00:06:46.448 --> 00:06:49.325
but aren't you guys missing a member?

00:06:49.826 --> 00:06:51.202
You're the top ten,

00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:53.329
but there are only nine of you.

00:06:55.457 --> 00:06:57.000
I'm right here.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.051
Now there are ten.

00:07:07.677 --> 00:07:10.430
Well, do your best.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.323
Tennis prodigy Ikuto Kimijima.

00:07:29.783 --> 00:07:31.951
What does he go for after playing sports?

00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:35.955
Let this moisten your lips, too.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.794
He's that first string guy we saw on the court!

00:07:41.586 --> 00:07:44.130
Did you see that, Marui-<i>san</i>?

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.716
Yeah, they're all star players.

00:07:47.092 --> 00:07:49.761
Huh? Marui-<i>san</i>, where are you going?

00:07:50.679 --> 00:07:51.763
For a walk.

00:07:57.394 --> 00:07:59.938
You're keeping a pretty fast pace, Kaidoh.

00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:01.898
If you don't hydrate,
you'll exhaust yourself.

00:08:01.898 --> 00:08:03.483
Don't worry about me.

00:08:03.858 --> 00:08:07.487
I've got a drink on that bench.

00:08:09.656 --> 00:08:10.490
Mine!

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:13.410
Hey! That's my drink!

00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:16.871
Damn. Who was that guy?

00:08:17.831 --> 00:08:22.252
Ah, a two-wheeled electric
vehicle. How tasteful.

00:08:22.711 --> 00:08:24.963
Calm down, Kaoru Kaidoh.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.924
I have a hydration spot up ahead.

00:08:27.924 --> 00:08:29.592
Just hold out until we get there.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.680
Listen, Kaidoh.

00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:38.101
They say advice is good,
but patience is better.

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:41.104
It's important to listen to advice,

00:08:41.104 --> 00:08:44.607
but nothing is more important
than to have patience.

00:08:47.777 --> 00:08:49.487
That's my hydration--

00:08:50.405 --> 00:08:51.781
This is mine, too!

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.201
That's No. 2, Tanegashima!

00:08:55.952 --> 00:08:57.787
Stop right there!

00:09:01.124 --> 00:09:05.337
With no trump card, I can't play in matches.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:11.051
If I don't play in matches, I can't
demonstrate Okinawa's strength.

00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:15.221
I need to make sure I can
land the final checkmate.

00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:28.610
Whew, that was close.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:30.236
Nice catch.

00:09:36.743 --> 00:09:39.621
Feel like playing some tennis?

00:09:41.956 --> 00:09:43.416
What a coincidence.

00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:45.794
I'm in the mood to work up a sweat myself.

00:09:58.723 --> 00:09:59.766
Hey...

00:10:00.058 --> 00:10:03.853
Why did you ask me to practice with you?

00:10:14.322 --> 00:10:15.865
We'll start with five.

00:10:30.588 --> 00:10:33.174
Looks like you're getting warmed up.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.593
I'll add two more.

00:10:38.596 --> 00:10:41.391
You can add five more.

00:10:48.732 --> 00:10:51.651
Hey, Tokugawa-<i>san</i>, you said you were

00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:53.862
on the court at the top of the cliff last year.

00:10:56.698 --> 00:10:59.701
Did that bearded guy beat you?

00:11:03.038 --> 00:11:04.289
Ryoma Echizen,

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:07.250
is there anyone you'd give
your own life to beat?

00:11:12.088 --> 00:11:12.964
For me...

00:11:14.382 --> 00:11:17.302
Ever since I was five,

00:11:17.302 --> 00:11:21.890
I trained overseas every day
to become a professional.

00:11:28.563 --> 00:11:29.773
One year ago,

00:11:30.607 --> 00:11:33.902
I was at my peak,
winning match after match.

00:11:33.902 --> 00:11:35.695
I feared no one.

00:11:37.364 --> 00:11:41.493
That's when I was invited
to this training camp.

00:11:42.827 --> 00:11:43.870
At the time,

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:48.208
Japan's junior players didn't
stand a chance on the world stage.

00:11:49.042 --> 00:11:49.709
Frankly,

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:53.630
the training they were
doing here seemed juvenile.

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:56.800
That's how clear the difference felt.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:00.720
I underestimated this training camp.

00:12:09.521 --> 00:12:10.772
Until...

00:12:11.356 --> 00:12:14.526
that man crushed my pride to dust.

00:12:18.446 --> 00:12:21.199
Sorry for keeping you out so late.

00:12:23.034 --> 00:12:24.119
Want some?

00:12:25.078 --> 00:12:26.079
Thanks.

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:27.455
Scatter.

00:12:42.262 --> 00:12:43.054
Tokugawa-<i>san</i>!

00:12:47.142 --> 00:12:49.686
You protected this little boy?

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.396
Fool.

00:12:54.357 --> 00:12:56.818
Hey, you know what?

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.490
Let's play right now.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.075
I know I'll win, though.

00:13:07.495 --> 00:13:08.913
Perish!

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:42.489
You can't beat him.

00:13:43.198 --> 00:13:45.492
Who are you, anyway?

00:13:46.618 --> 00:13:49.454
It's been a while, shorty.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:51.873
It's me.

00:13:52.248 --> 00:13:53.792
Ryoga Echizen.

00:13:58.421 --> 00:13:59.339
Who?

00:13:59.339 --> 00:14:00.131
Hey!

00:14:02.759 --> 00:14:06.388
Don't tell me you forgot your own brother.

00:14:17.148 --> 00:14:20.151
This training camp is getting pretty crazy.

00:14:21.945 --> 00:14:25.448
Isn't our Rookie of the West amazing, Yushi?

00:14:25.448 --> 00:14:27.659
What are you talking about, Kenya?

00:14:27.659 --> 00:14:31.079
The Rookie of the East
picked a fight with No. 1.

00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:33.998
Well, I say the West is better!

00:14:34.749 --> 00:14:35.667
No, the East!

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:36.668
West!

00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:37.585
East!

00:14:37.585 --> 00:14:38.670
West!

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.005
You don't get it, do you?

00:14:40.005 --> 00:14:42.215
If I say East, it's East!

00:14:42.215 --> 00:14:43.842
You're the one who doesn't get it!

00:14:43.842 --> 00:14:45.760
I say it's West, so it's West!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.680
"Niou Kingdom"
"Niou      Kabaji"

00:14:51.474 --> 00:14:52.726
Is Niou here?

00:14:58.898 --> 00:15:01.109
Time for bed...

00:15:01.943 --> 00:15:04.029
Did you know, Kuwahara-<i>kun</i>?

00:15:05.196 --> 00:15:11.453
Today, Marui-<i>kun </i>was having fun practicing
with the captain of Higa's team.

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:16.791
Don't say that, Yagyuu-<i>san</i>!

00:15:17.834 --> 00:15:19.502
He was having fun?

00:15:19.502 --> 00:15:20.712
You're upset about <i>that</i>?!

00:15:22.339 --> 00:15:24.883
Here we go, Marui-<i>kun</i>!

00:15:24.883 --> 00:15:27.177
Yeah! I'm ready any time!

00:15:27.469 --> 00:15:28.595
There!

00:15:28.887 --> 00:15:30.013
There!

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.276
Fire!

00:15:43.943 --> 00:15:46.863
That's not good... Not good at all...

00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:25.068
You can't beat him.

00:16:26.945 --> 00:16:28.363
Sounds interesting.

00:17:03.857 --> 00:17:06.359
It's finally started running.

00:17:08.528 --> 00:17:10.905
There's no stopping it now.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:16.995
There we go.

00:17:19.914 --> 00:17:22.542
Things are starting to get fun.

00:17:37.474 --> 00:17:38.475
A match?

00:17:39.434 --> 00:17:41.311
Who's playing at this hour?

00:17:47.442 --> 00:17:49.611
Oni, you're...

00:17:49.986 --> 00:17:52.238
...even stronger than the Black Jack Knife...

00:17:52.655 --> 00:17:54.991
Sorry, Kaji.

00:17:55.784 --> 00:17:58.036
I'm taking this back.

00:17:59.871 --> 00:18:01.373
So that's it.

00:18:03.083 --> 00:18:05.877
Court 5, Jujiroh Oni.

00:18:07.128 --> 00:18:09.047
How long have you been standing there?

00:18:09.047 --> 00:18:09.798
Who knows?

00:18:14.302 --> 00:18:15.679
Coach Nyudo...

00:18:22.185 --> 00:18:25.397
He sent you guys burial clothes?

00:18:26.064 --> 00:18:29.818
For that old man,
that's quite a thoughtful gift.

00:18:31.069 --> 00:18:33.071
Burial clothes, huh?

00:18:51.631 --> 00:18:54.676
Echizen, that jersey...

00:18:57.137 --> 00:18:59.639
It's a gift from Coach Nyudo.

00:19:00.348 --> 00:19:02.100
From that bearded coach?

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.060
I thought he buried them.

00:19:05.687 --> 00:19:07.022
Here it is!

00:19:07.022 --> 00:19:08.189
It's my jersey!

00:19:13.069 --> 00:19:16.531
They're our burial clothes, apparently.

00:19:17.699 --> 00:19:19.409
Who said that?

00:19:19.409 --> 00:19:20.785
Jujiroh Oni.

00:19:21.578 --> 00:19:26.458
Apparently he beat No. 5
and joined the first string.

00:19:28.335 --> 00:19:31.713
Hey, what are burial clothes?

00:19:32.047 --> 00:19:34.007
Burial clothes?

00:19:34.007 --> 00:19:35.300
Don't be absurd!

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:37.635
Calm down, Kaoru Kaidoh.

00:19:38.011 --> 00:19:40.555
Oni-<i>san </i>doesn't mince words.

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:44.476
Yeah, but we can't just take this lying down.

00:19:45.143 --> 00:19:48.146
We'll have to show them ourselves

00:19:48.688 --> 00:19:53.443
whether or not these are burial clothes.

00:20:06.373 --> 00:20:10.377
Hey, Koshimae! What are burial clothes?

00:20:10.377 --> 00:20:10.752
Come on.

00:20:12.212 --> 00:20:15.173
I'll tell you later. Just go get changed.

00:20:16.341 --> 00:20:19.135
Well, that just sounds perfect, huh?

00:20:27.435 --> 00:20:29.604
Quit lollygagging!

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:32.649
Gather 'round right now!

00:20:33.942 --> 00:20:38.113
Oni-<i>kun </i>has returned to his former position.

00:20:38.113 --> 00:20:38.863
Yeah.

00:20:39.698 --> 00:20:43.451
And those middle schoolers' jerseys...

00:20:43.827 --> 00:20:45.245
They're at a rebellious age.

00:20:50.458 --> 00:20:54.629
Now everyone's where they belong.

00:20:55.714 --> 00:20:58.049
It's time.

00:20:59.676 --> 00:21:03.430
The first U-17 Japanese team versus

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:07.976
second string shuffle match will now begin.

00:21:08.351 --> 00:21:10.478
Representing the U-17 Japanese team are

00:21:10.478 --> 00:21:17.193
doubles team No. 10, Jusaburoh Mori,
and No. 9, Tsukimitsu Ochi.

00:21:22.699 --> 00:21:24.743
I'm up first!

00:21:25.035 --> 00:21:26.661
He's playing doubles?

00:21:27.328 --> 00:21:29.247
Who's his partner?

00:21:30.749 --> 00:21:32.542
Let's go, Niou!

00:21:33.293 --> 00:21:35.253
I've been waiting for this.

00:21:36.212 --> 00:21:37.630
Representing the second string are

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:40.175
Keigo Atobe and Masaharu Niou.

00:21:43.178 --> 00:21:45.764
Keep your guard up, Atobe.

00:23:18.398 --> 00:23:19.274
"Next Time"

00:23:19.274 --> 00:23:21.484
"Next Time"
Why aren't my Tannhausers working?

00:23:21.484 --> 00:23:22.068
Why aren't my Tannhausers working?

00:23:22.068 --> 00:23:23.111
Damn it!

00:23:23.111 --> 00:23:25.405
What's wrong, Atobe? This isn't like you.

00:23:25.405 --> 00:23:26.990
Don't panic.

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.158
Shut up!

00:23:28.158 --> 00:23:31.286
It's impossible for me not to win this point!

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:34.706
Atobe, you don't need
to hit the ball anymore.

00:23:34.706 --> 00:23:35.749
What?

00:23:35.749 --> 00:23:38.251
I'll deflect the rest out of the court.

00:23:41.171 --> 00:23:42.714
"The Strongest Pair"
The next episode of <i>New Prince</i>
<i>of Tennis </i>is: "The Strongest Pair."

00:23:42.714 --> 00:23:45.842
"The Strongest Pair"
You're not fighting alone.

00:23:45.842 --> 00:23:48.480
"The Strongest Pair"
This is a doubles match.
